<section class="section section--alt" id="sql">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Python or SQL</p>
      <h2>The same plan, either way.</h2>
      <p class="lede">The DataFrame API and SQL build the same logical plan, so they run through the same optimizer and the same execution engine. Query with an expressive DataFrame API or clean analytical SQL.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid--2" data-reveal-stagger>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card__top">
          <h3>DataFrame</h3>
          <span class="card__tag">Python · Lazy</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="code"><span class="fn">lf</span> = iara.<span class="fn">scan_parquet</span>(<span class="str">"s3://bucket/events/"</span>)
<span class="fn">top</span> = (
    lf.<span class="fn">filter</span>(F.<span class="fn">col</span>(<span class="str">"country"</span>) == <span class="str">"BR"</span>)
      .<span class="fn">group_by</span>(<span class="str">"page"</span>)
      .<span class="fn">agg</span>(views=F.<span class="fn">len</span>())
      .<span class="fn">sort</span>(<span class="str">"views"</span>, descending=<span class="kw">True</span>)
      .<span class="fn">head</span>(<span class="num">10</span>)
)
top.<span class="fn">collect</span>()</pre>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="card__top">
          <h3>SQL</h3>
          <span class="card__tag">Analytical SQL</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="code">iara.<span class="fn">sql</span>(<span class="str">"""
    select page, count(*) as views
    from read_parquet('s3://bucket/events/')
    where country = 'BR'
    group by page
    order by views desc
    limit 10
"""</span>)</pre>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="small muted note" data-reveal>Inputs can also be pyarrow tables, pandas or Polars DataFrames: <code>iara.sql("select k, sum(v) from t group by k", t=arrow_table)</code>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

